{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1002546-fixing-combat","id":1002546,"title":"Fixing Combat","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-13T09:39:33-08:00","id":1002546,"title":"Fixing Combat","content":"I was wondering what fixes that people use for making the combat rules for WoD actually work. For example, in my games, I make combat a static difficulty '6' and, instead of decreasing or increasing difficulty, I increase or decrease die pools (if a technique would have a base difficulty below '6' or a base difficulty above '6', I give a die pool bonus or penalty equal to the difference). I separate defensive and offensive die pools, so characters roll their entire defensive die pool (minus one per previous attack defended against during the same turn), which allows players to take risks and reduces the imbalance creation by Celerity, Rage, etc (Celerity, Rage, etc allows players to take extra attacks and extra movements, rather than extra actions). Normal movement occurs during the attack phase and, with each extra attack, a player can take extra movement.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T13:45:32-08:00","id":1002628,"title":"","content":"I think there needs to be a set idea of what you consider wrong with the system before you can just jump in and change stuff and make it work. Mechanically speaking, combat in the WoD (though there are differences between the editions and the game lines even in the 20th era, so pinning any of that down is hard) does actually work. How it works just isn't satisfying to a lot of people; but they don't all have the same issues.<br /> <br /> Part of the issue is that a lot of things I think could improve things don't necessarily work well for every game-line.<br /> <br /> For example, I would love to see WtA move to a popcorn style initiative system because it's a massive improvement in the realms of pack-tactics over traditional initiative (with or without the declaration phase). However, I don't feel nearly as strongly about popcorn initiative for the other games (if anything, I'd love to move away from the traditional + declare model for something more like Exalted 3e's traditional + Initiative damage system).<br /> <br /> Of course, both of those would be massive overhauls compared to things like you've suggested.<br /> <br /> Some smaller (or at least less of a need to rewrite wide swathes of the game) stuff I'd do:<br /> <br /> 1) I think DAV20 was on the right track with one attack per round and have Celerity be a mix of reducing multiple action penalties and increasing your number of attacks cap. It simplifies extra action powers significantly and makes them easier to counter without neutering them.<br /> <br /> 2) Instead of having an offense and defense pool to split up as you want, I'd favor moving towards static defenses (so soak as well) with the option to roll for &quot;special&quot; defenses. So you have some base Defense Value if you're just trying avoid the hit, but if you want to parry with the option to disarm or riposte you roll and it cuts into your main action dice-pool (possibly with penalties to your DV for the rest of the round as well).<br /> <br /> 3) Take an ax to the massive maneuver list. The number of maneuvers are insane, and frequently redundant. The differences between a punch and a kick are not worth having two maneuvers. Put all that word count into a better guide towards adjudicating how to apply bonuses/penalties to the intent of an action so players can say, &quot;I want to knockdown my opponent,&quot; without having to figure out which of the multiple maneuvers that can result in this is the best for what they're after. Basically I see this as a big source of decision paralysis that adds little to the game.<br /> <br /> 4) Dump the weapon and armor lists. Take a few pages from Ex3 and other games and just have a few basic templates that you modify with a tag system. Less to remember, less hunting and pecking for the optimal weapon, less hassle adding weapons that the books don't cover, etc. Again, cut down on play decision making that doesn't really add much. Also take the chance to make armor less mediocre. Also abstract ammo instead of carrying about clip sizes.<br /> <br /> 5) Use the DA Revised multiple action order system instead of the weird, normal action first, Celerity/Rage/etc. actions at the end (though less of an issue if you do #1). <br /> <br /> 6) Abstract range bands over nebulous distances. CofD's Hurt Locker is going to include a whole section on doing this and how to work in the extant movement rates of that game just like you'd need to do with WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T17:17:26-08:00","id":1002710,"title":"","content":"I second most of what Heavy Arms said. Would only add that I would get rid of multiple actions completely, and substitute for bonuses that could be linked to velocity in some way.<br /> <br /> Actually I'm not used to &quot;fix&quot; the WoD system, since usually CoD works a lot better as a system for me. When system is a concern for me, I adapt what I want from WoD to CoD's system, and that's it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T11:26:15-08:00","id":1002975,"title":"","content":"I eliminate many rolls. Especially in combat.<br /> <br /> Take this example:<br /> Ben Brujah dances circles around his opponent, he feints left, then right and throws himself in a spinning hurricane kick.<br /> Walther Wendigo saw it coming and manages to catch the kick. But the force knocks his hand back right in his face.<br /> He snarls and throws Ben towards the next wall.<br /> <br /> Now count the dice rolls of this incomplete turn with two participants.<br /> <br /> Even if we just take the first attack and the block we get FOUR.<br /> Now consider positioning, feints and the rest of the Players all with multiple Actions and you get something like 8 rolls per second game time.<br /> Bullet Time is a newborn cub compared to this.<br /> <br /> The declare actions step slows the crawl further.<br /> <br /> How are you supposed to be able to TELL a action filled, immersive STORY with these clunky mechanics?<br /> <br /> So I cut the soak for starters, the action declaring step was an instant dislike anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T18:15:50-08:00","id":1003177,"title":"","content":"Declaring actions has always been a poor system that was required because players had to choose between attacking or actively defending. If you have a reflexive defense system (where the defense die pool is independent of the attack die pool), then you do not have to declare actions, you can just attack and defend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T00:30:59-08:00","id":1003273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1002546-fixing-combat?p=1003177#post1003177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Declaring actions has always been a poor system that was required because players had to choose between attacking or actively defending. If you have a reflexive defense system (where the defense die pool is independent of the attack die pool), then you do not have to declare actions, you can just attack and defend.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your solution is fine if it works for you, but I don't like it because it adds another roll bringing the total up to something like 12 rolls per second game time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T06:15:53-08:00","id":1003352,"title":"","content":"Then create passive defenses and soaks to serve as a minimum threshold for success or damage. A passive defense threshold would be (modified defense die pool \u00f7 2, rounded up, +1). A passive soak threshold would be (modified soak die pool \u00f7 2, rounded up, +1). You could just have players make a table that ranges from +5 to -5 die pool modifiers to allow for quick reference. Each players would then only have to make two rolls per turn, attack and damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T06:20:45-08:00","id":1003354,"title":"","content":"This is how I do it.<br /> But I subtract the defense/soak dicepool from the corresponding attacker's pool.<br /> Statistically the same at difficulty 6.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T12:11:49-08:00","id":1003531,"title":"","content":"Minor nit-pick (since I generally agree with that approach): the odds of net successes is the same. The odds of failure, the odds of botching, and the odds of lucky big hits change significantly.<br /> <br /> 8 dice vs 4 dice in a roll has low odds of botching, low odds of outright failure before the defender even rolls (which can impact things like parry and rebound damage), and theoretically could score up to 16 successes (all 10s with a specialty).<br /> <br /> 4 dice dramatically increases the odds of outright failure/botch, and your maximum possible successes is cut to 8.<br /> <br /> The increase in fail/botch rates can make combat drag because the average damage output goes down; resulting in more rolls because it takes more turns. There's also the issue of a character having high enough defenses that they can reduce attacks to 0, which is an automatic failure as well which can stalemate or drag on fights as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T12:35:44-08:00","id":1003539,"title":"","content":"Increasing the threshold of successes required tends to deal with both of those issues as, even if someone fails to hit the threshold, they will still generate successes and will not botch. For example, if you had two characters, each with 10 dice to attack and defend, you would end up with 0 dice in attacks on both sides if you subtract defense pools from attack rolls, giving a 0% chance of success on both sides. If, however, defense die pools instead modify thresholds, then each would roll 10 dice against a threshold of 6, giving around a 30% of success with each attack. The same thing would apply with soak rolls, subtraction would result in 0 dice for damage while increasing thresholds would give around a 30% chance of one health level of damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T13:09:04-08:00","id":1003556,"title":"","content":"These are the things i want to see in a combat system (though i have no idea how to implement it):<br /> -Two rolls, one for the aggressor and one for the defender.<br /> -Standard action is to avoid damage if attacked (spend WP to ignore instinct and attack, knowing full well you'll take damage, otherwise abort stated action to defend).<br /> -Multiple actions are standard (seriously, you dont throw one punch every 3 seconds unless all out swing, you have a flurry of strikes and blocks from both parties in that timeframe). Defensive actions are incorporated in this. One could forego all multiple actions for one giant strike/swing/whatever. This grants bonus dice at the cost of a WP (see previous point).<br /> -Better weapons and armor rules. Armor shouldn't just add dice to soak. I've seen threads here about ballistics vests converting Lethal to Bashing for bullets. More of this please. And make sure that weapons do a realistic type and amount of damage (i'm looking at you Warhammer that does Bashing).<br /> -Make Aggravated Damage rare and make it hurt more. To me, Agg should only be Banes (Fire, Sun and Faith) for vampires, Pattern Damage for Mage and Silver for Werewolf. All other forms of agg should either be downgraded to lethal or have their own fourth category.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T14:13:46-08:00","id":1003597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cadmiumcadamium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1002546-fixing-combat?p=1003556#post1003556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These are the things i want to see in a combat system (though i have no idea how to implement it):</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of this could be taken from CofD 2e, Storypath, or Ex3 since they all use a similar base-line.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -Standard action is to avoid damage if attacked (spend WP to ignore instinct and attack, knowing full well you'll take damage, otherwise abort stated action to defend). </div> </div> </div>I'm not quite sure what you mean here. You have to spend 1 WP to do anything but defend yourself? Or that rather than the current rules of spend 1 WP to abort to defend, you automatically abort to defend and you have to spend 1 WP not to defend?<br /> <br /> Either case seems like it could get funky, esp. with the assumption of a default instinct of defense over offense. The idea of a Crinos Garou having the instinct to defend against a normal human punch seems a bit absurd.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -Multiple actions are standard (seriously, you dont throw one punch every 3 seconds unless all out swing, you have a flurry of strikes and blocks from both parties in that timeframe). Defensive actions are incorporated in this. One could forego all multiple actions for one giant strike/swing/whatever. This grants bonus dice at the cost of a WP (see previous point). </div> </div> </div>I think it's easier to work on making things more abstract. Make the default assumption that one &quot;attack&quot; in a combat round is whatever you want it to be. It could be one carefully placed shot, or a flurry of blows meant to try to get a solid hit through. Moving away from the idea that one roll = one physical attack makes a lot of things a lot easier.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T19:24:51-08:00","id":1003743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cadmiumcadamium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1002546-fixing-combat?p=1003556#post1003556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Make Aggravated Damage rare and make it hurt more. To me, Agg should only be Banes (Fire, Sun and Faith) for vampires, Pattern Damage for Mage and Silver for Werewolf. All other forms of agg should either be downgraded to lethal or have their own fourth category.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rare agg is one of the dividing lines between the feel of the CoD and WoD. Making it the standard for the WoD just wouldn't feel right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T20:26:15-08:00","id":1003762,"title":"","content":"A 4th category of damage would just be excessive (heck, three is a bit excessive).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}